WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.036
-Today, the Justice Department

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.570
released Attorney General
William Barr's

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.205
redacted version
of Special Counsel

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:07.473
Robert Mueller's final report.

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:10.309
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:13.879
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.782
Well, it's finally here.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.250
We finally have
a redacted version of the thing

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.653
that everyone in Washington
has been anxiously awaiting

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.922
for almost two years,
and for two years,

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.891
the media
has been obsessively dissecting

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.059
every morsel of information
or speculation

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:28.495
about the investigation.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:31.397
There was even the time Mueller
was spotted at the airport

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.867
at the same gate as Don Jr.,
and pundits speculated

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:37.536
about everything from his
clothes to where he was going.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.572
-We're about
to have a wow moment.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.275
Stand by.
We now have the photo.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.777
This was taken by Politico.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:46.745
This is Reagan airport
in Washington, D.C.

00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:49.181
The man spotlighted
on the left side of your screen

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:51.951
just sitting there, hanging out,
this is Robert Mueller.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:55.021
This is the special counsel
who is the one we've been saying

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.624
knows way more than we all do.
-You know, it's interesting.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.325
So, having worked
for Bob Mueller,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.662
I know that he has two ties,
a red one and a blue one.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.631
-Are we really
getting into the ties?

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:06.699
-It looks as though --

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.167
I'd be curious
to see where he's headed.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.870
Is he taking a little vacation,
which is probably much deserved,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.038
or is he going
to hunt for more clues?

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:16.576
-They were speculating
over the ties he wears.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.378
Blue tie means Trump's innocent,
red tie means he's guilty,

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.813
and no tie means Robert Mueller

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.183
is ready
for a night out on the town.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.217
Also, he probably
wasn't going anywhere.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.052
I bet Robert Mueller
goes to the airport

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:29.556
just because he likes
going through security.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:30.589
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:31.958
"All right,
you're all good, sir."

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.460
"Scan me again -- for safety."

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.261
And on top of that,
we've been living through months

00:01:36.261 --> 00:01:37.496
of endless speculation

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:40.099
about when the investigation
would finally end.

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:43.102
In fact, the media specifically
kept speculating about

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:46.305
whether the investigation
was wrapping up or winding down.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:48.107
-Do you see Mueller
wrapping this up

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:49.976
at any point in the near future?

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.310
-When you read the tea leaves,

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.013
this could mean that the probe
is actually winding down.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:58.585
-That multifaceted investigation
may be wrapping up soon.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.786
-That could very well signal

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:02.421
that the investigation
is, indeed, winding down.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:05.124
-Does this mean Mueller's
getting close to wrapping up?

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.326
-The investigation
appears to be winding down.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:08.695
-Maybe this thing
is wrapping up.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.896
-This could be winding down.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.564
-It may be close to wrapping up.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.067
-Potentially, the investigation
is winding down.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.069
-That right there is my favorite
House of Pain song.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:19.672
♪ Wrap it up, wind it down,
jerk us around ♪

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.073
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.241
They've been saying
the Mueller report

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.709
was about to come out forever.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.111
In fact, true story --
when they found

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.313
those 20,000-year-old
cave paintings in France,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:30.316
one of them just said,
"Is Mueller wrapping up?"

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.286
Now the report is finally here,
but before he even had any idea

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.154
what was in the report,
Trump spent weeks

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.956
declaring victory and setting
incredibly high expectations

00:02:37.956 --> 00:02:40.360
for how the full report
would totally and completely

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.660
vindicate him of everything,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.331
with one small caveat that comes
at the very, very end.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.768
-It was a complete
and total exoneration.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.903
The Mueller report was great.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:52.371
It could not have been better.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.206
The finding
was very, very strong --

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:59.144
no collusion, no obstruction,
no Russia, no nothing.

00:02:59.144 --> 00:03:00.546
The result was great.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:04.950
No obstruction, no collusion,
no anything.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:10.023
Total exoneration.
Complete vindication.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.757
Everybody waited
for the Mueller report,

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.793
but then it turns out
that there's no obstruction,

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:16.863
no collusion, no anything.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:19.966
I won.
No collusion, no obstruction.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.034
I won.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.435
I have not read
the Mueller report.

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:26.005
I haven't seen
the Mueller report.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.540
As far as I'm concerned,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.909
I don't care
about the Mueller report.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.478
-"The Mueller report is great.
It exonerates me.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.380
I've never read it.
I don't care about it."

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.781
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:38.617
You're like a terrible boyfriend
who keeps giving mixed messages.

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:39.952
"I love you, but I need space,

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:41.754
and I can't live without you,
but you're crowding me."

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.088
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:46.225
In fact, Trump even said
he was being charitable to us

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.826
by not overreacting.

00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:49.228
-It's a disgrace what happened.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:52.198
And, again, it should never
happen to a president again.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.199
You're just lucky I happen to be
the president.

00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:57.370
Because a lot of other
presidents would have reacted

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.271
much differently than I reacted.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.673
-That's kind of true.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.875
I mean, it really only happened
to one other president,

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.611
and he quit.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.080
Now, before we get
into the report,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.781
let's just review
what we already know.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.516
For one thing,
Mueller has already produced

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.585
a staggering number
of indictments and convictions

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.754
of some of the President's
closest aides and advisers.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.155
I mean, look at this --

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:19.759
this group has more criminals in
it than a Hollywood PTA meeting.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.960
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.429
Two, even before
we got the report today,

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.232
Trump was already
directly implicated

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:29.435
in a crime to break election law
during the 2016 campaign

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.938
by paying hush money
to cover up an affair.

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.806
Of course,
as you might remember,

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.242
prosecutors mysteriously
referred to him

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.745
as Individual #1
in the court filing

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:42.014
despite also telling us that
Individual #1

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:44.217
"began an ultimately
successful campaign

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.285
for President
of the United States."

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.654
And then, in a big,
dramatic reveal,

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.156
Trump's ex-lawyer,
Michael Cohen,

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:53.025
revealed to the world
who Individual #1 was.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:57.062
-Last fall, I pled guilty
in federal court

00:04:57.062 --> 00:05:01.967
to felonies for the benefit of,
at the direction of,

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:07.806
and in coordination with
Individual #1.

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:11.710
And for the record,
Individual #1

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:16.081
is President Donald J. Trump.

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:18.985
-Yeah, dude, we know.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:22.288
That was, like, the easiest
"Where's Waldo?" of all time.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.990
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.791
So, what we already knew
was damning,

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:27.860
and even Trump's inner circle
seemed to know the report

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.529
might be damning,
which might explain

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.230
why their handling of the report
was so weird.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.400
First, Barr issued his infamous
letter summarizing the report.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.201
Then, a week later,
he issued a second letter

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:38.171
saying the first letter
wasn't supposed to be a summary.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.838
Then, Mueller's team
started leaking

00:05:39.838 --> 00:05:41.674
and saying they weren't happy
with Barr's summary.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.475
Then, we found out
they wrote their own summaries

00:05:43.475 --> 00:05:44.944
that Barr didn't use.

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:47.179
Then we found out Barr briefed
the White House on the report.

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:48.413
Then we found out Barr let

00:05:48.413 --> 00:05:49.915
Trump's attorneys
see the report.

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:53.552
I mean, Jesus, who else got
to see this thing before us?

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:56.355
"I don't know.
I, uh...

00:05:56.355 --> 00:06:02.761
I feel like it really..."
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:04.496
I feel like
I come off as bad guy.

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:06.733
Where are my Sharpie?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:09.201
Then, this morning, Barr held
a press conference on the report

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:11.337
where he spun
all the conclusions

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.839
before reporters or the public

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.540
actually had a chance
to read the report.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.808
No one had read it.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.444
Well, some people had read it,
as Barr explained.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:21.614
-Earlier this week,
the President's personal counsel

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:24.884
requested and was given
the opportunity to read

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:27.720
a final version
of the redacted report

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.988
before it was publicly released.

00:06:29.988 --> 00:06:31.457
-That means Rudy Giuliani

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.525
got to read the report
before the rest of us.

00:06:33.525 --> 00:06:36.729
And from the looks of it,
he was trying to open his eyes

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:40.533
wide enough
to read all 400 pages at once.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.434
"I don't like to flip.
Spread them all out."

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:47.773
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:51.878
Now, on the question of the
Trump campaign's ties to Russia,

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:54.980
the Mueller report says the
investigation also identified

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.882
numerous links between
the Russian government

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:58.283
and the Trump campaign.

00:06:58.283 --> 00:07:00.319
But in his press conference,
Barr chose instead

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.121
to highlight a sentence
from his report

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:03.689
that he knew
would please his boss

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.223
and repeated it over and over.

00:07:05.223 --> 00:07:08.961
-The Special Counsel's report
states that his

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:11.096
"investigation did not establish

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:13.032
that members
of the Trump campaign

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:16.802
conspired or coordinated
with the Russian government.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:20.306
The Russian operatives
who perpetrated these schemes

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:22.642
did not have the cooperation

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:25.477
of President Trump
or the Trump campaign."

00:07:25.477 --> 00:07:29.482
The Special Counsel found
no evidence that any American,

00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:32.852
including anyone associated
with the Trump campaign,

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:36.054
conspired or coordinated
with the Russian government.

00:07:36.054 --> 00:07:39.925
Again, the Special Counsel's
report did not find any evidence

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:41.760
that members
of the Trump campaign

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:44.664
or anyone associated
with the campaign,

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:47.866
conspired or coordinated
with the Russian government.

00:07:47.866 --> 00:07:49.568
As he said from the beginning,

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:52.538
there was, in fact,
no collusion.

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:54.306
-My God, halfway through that
press conference,

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:56.608
I started expecting Barr
to rip off his mask

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:58.511
and reveal it was Trump
the whole time.

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:00.178
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.178 --> 00:08:01.313
The Mueller investigation

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:03.315
had questions
it was supposed to answer.

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:05.284
Now we have the report.
We can take our time

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:07.886
and go through and hopefully
get answers to those questions.

00:08:07.886 --> 00:08:10.022
And on top of that,
the guy who wrote the report,

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:12.024
the guy who almost never
speaks publicly,

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.292
Robert Mueller himself,

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:16.128
might actually testify
in public before Congress.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.996
-Jerry Nadler,
who is the chairman

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:19.531
of the House
Committee on the Judiciary,

00:08:19.531 --> 00:08:22.835
has now formally requested that
the Honorable Robert Mueller,

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:26.238
the Special Counsel,
come and testify before Congress

00:08:26.238 --> 00:08:28.273
no later than May 23rd.

00:08:28.273 --> 00:08:30.609
-Wow, we might actually
hear from Robert Mueller.

00:08:30.609 --> 00:08:32.678
He never speaks in public.

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:34.880
Honestly, I don't even know
what his voice sounds like.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.549
For all I know, he could sound
like Bobcat Goldthwait,

00:08:37.549 --> 00:08:40.286
or maybe his mouth moves
like a "South Park" character.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.254
-You will respect my authoritah!

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:43.455
[ Laughter ]

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:45.991
-We don't know.

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:47.993
So once Barr was done
with his press conference,

00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:50.095
Congress and reporters
finally started

00:08:50.095 --> 00:08:51.630
to get their hands
on the report,

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.000
but the way they got the report
was as weird as everything else

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.001
about how Trump's team
handled the process.

00:08:56.001 --> 00:08:59.071
-Good morning, everyone.
So, here's how this plays out.

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:02.741
First, Congress gets the report
delivered this morning on CD.

00:09:02.741 --> 00:09:07.013
-Now, we have this interregnum
for 45 more minutes

00:09:07.013 --> 00:09:10.048
before members of Congress
and, of course,

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:12.084
the members of the public
are allowed to see

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:14.953
the CD-ROM of this report.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:17.056
-Any minute now,
we are expecting

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:20.525
a Justice Department official
to come and drop off a disk

00:09:20.525 --> 00:09:23.695
of the redacted report to the
House Judiciary Committee.

00:09:23.695 --> 00:09:26.432
We are expecting, Jake,
in a matter of moments

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:28.300
the disk to be dropped off.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.903
-That's right --
a compact disk.

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:34.473
They got the Mueller report
the same way we all got Encarta.

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:35.674
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.674 --> 00:09:37.843
Seriously, this is how
the government handles

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:40.913
one of the most anticipated
documents in recent history?

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:43.949
Was it a report or did they just
send Congress a mixtape?

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:49.488
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:52.558
The fact is, reporters were
waiting for this disk to arrive.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:54.026
Everyone was literally
sitting on

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:56.261
the Justice Department website
reloading the page

00:09:56.261 --> 00:09:58.096
where the report
was supposed to be posted.

00:09:58.096 --> 00:10:02.902
-It is up, is online.
You can go to www.justice.gov,

00:10:02.902 --> 00:10:07.139
and I think it's
/storage/report.pdf.

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:09.541
-We're just waiting
to find out more.

00:10:09.541 --> 00:10:12.778
I'm sure everyone is eagerly
hitting the refresh button

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.814
on the Department of Justice
website.

00:10:14.814 --> 00:10:16.482
-Oh, good.
So the same way people see

00:10:16.482 --> 00:10:17.950
if they got
their Coachella tickets.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.118
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:21.553
Also, can we hear that
website link again?

00:10:21.553 --> 00:10:24.790
-You can go to www.justice.gov,

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.961
and I think it's
/storage/report.pdf.

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:32.398
-My God, that link constitutes
obstruction of justice.

00:10:32.398 --> 00:10:33.532
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.532 --> 00:10:36.301
Just buy MuellerReport.gov
or something.

00:10:36.301 --> 00:10:38.404
If you're gonna make it hard
to find, why not go all the way

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:43.975
and post it at
justice.gov/storage/report
/no/collusion/innocent

00:10:43.975 --> 00:10:47.646
/witchhunt/dontlook
/stopclicking/whyareyouclicking

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:50.349
/messageboard/napster.biz?

00:10:50.349 --> 00:10:51.450
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:56.021
Still, now we have
the actual report.

00:10:56.021 --> 00:10:57.923
And suffice it to say,
it's a lot more damning

00:10:57.923 --> 00:11:00.259
and nuanced and legally dense
than Barr made it sound.

00:11:00.259 --> 00:11:02.094
For example,
on obstruction of justice,

00:11:02.094 --> 00:11:04.563
there's that question of whether
Trump had corrupt intent.

00:11:04.563 --> 00:11:07.532
Now, Republicans have been
chiding everyone else

00:11:07.532 --> 00:11:08.834
for thinking
Mueller's appointment

00:11:08.834 --> 00:11:10.536
would be the end
of Trump's presidency.

00:11:10.536 --> 00:11:12.437
They've been mocking people
for saying, "Oh, my God.

00:11:12.437 --> 00:11:13.372
This is the end
of his presidency.

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:14.673
He's [bleep]"

00:11:14.673 --> 00:11:16.942
But apparently, one of
the people who thought that

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:19.278
was Donald Trump himself,
because according to the report,

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:21.346
when his then
Attorney General Jeff Sessions

00:11:21.346 --> 00:11:22.814
told the president
that a Special Counsel

00:11:22.814 --> 00:11:24.282
had been appointed,
the President slumped back

00:11:24.282 --> 00:11:26.718
in his chair and said,
"Oh, my God. This is terrible.

00:11:26.718 --> 00:11:27.819
This is the end
of my presidency.

00:11:27.819 --> 00:11:29.754
I'm [bleep]"
[ Laughter ]

00:11:29.754 --> 00:11:36.295
Ugh! The one time we wanted you
to be right, and you weren't!

00:11:36.295 --> 00:11:38.597
No, while not surprising
to hear that even after all

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:40.232
of the new damning details
in the report,

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:41.900
the President,
who spent the last two weeks

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.902
calling it a total
and complete exoneration

00:11:43.902 --> 00:11:47.005
despite not reading it,
called the 400-page final report

00:11:47.005 --> 00:11:50.375
a total and complete exoneration
despite not reading it.

00:11:50.375 --> 00:11:52.778
-When I talked to people inside
the Trump campaign,

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:55.147
Trump advisers,
earlier this morning,

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:57.183
they just feel like
this is a complete victory.

00:11:57.183 --> 00:12:00.953
I talked to one Trump adviser
who said this is $40 million

00:12:00.953 --> 00:12:03.922
clean bill of health
for the President.

00:12:03.922 --> 00:12:06.058
-I'm sorry, but Donald Trump
has never in his life

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:07.693
gotten a clean bill of health.

00:12:07.693 --> 00:12:09.961
I mean, for one thing,
this is his doctor.

00:12:09.961 --> 00:12:12.130
[ Laughter ]
"Hey, good news, man.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:13.265
I did an X-ray.

00:12:13.265 --> 00:12:15.201
Most of your bones
are still there."

00:12:15.201 --> 00:12:16.601
[ Laughter ]

00:12:16.601 --> 00:12:18.236
Second, the report
is full of damning evidence

00:12:18.236 --> 00:12:19.671
about the President's
various attempts

00:12:19.671 --> 00:12:20.906
to influence the investigation.

00:12:20.906 --> 00:12:22.908
Mueller writes
that those attempts

00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:25.411
were mostly unsuccessful
largely because the persons

00:12:25.411 --> 00:12:27.980
who surrounded the President
declined to carry out orders.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:30.015
In fact, we've gotten
so many more details

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:32.150
about the campaign's
ties to Russia.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.686
Just take Trump's ex-campaign
chairman Paul Manafort

00:12:34.686 --> 00:12:36.155
as one example.

00:12:36.155 --> 00:12:39.058
Manafort communicated with the
Ukrainian political consultant

00:12:39.058 --> 00:12:42.027
tied to Russian intelligence
named Konstantin Kilimnik.

00:12:42.027 --> 00:12:43.996
Kilimnik proposed
a peace plan for Ukraine

00:12:43.996 --> 00:12:45.664
that Manafort
has since acknowledged

00:12:45.664 --> 00:12:48.768
was a backdoor means for Russia
to control Eastern Ukraine.

00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:50.769
Kilimnik wrote
an e-mail to Manafort,

00:12:50.769 --> 00:12:53.706
expressing the view which
Manafort later said he shared,

00:12:53.706 --> 00:12:57.042
that the plan's success would
require U.S. support to succeed.

00:12:57.042 --> 00:12:59.411
"All that is required
to start the process

00:12:59.411 --> 00:13:01.947
is a very minor wink
from Donald Trump."

00:13:01.947 --> 00:13:03.816
Of course, with Trump,
it's impossible to know

00:13:03.816 --> 00:13:06.452
if he's winking or just trying
to read off a teleprompter.

00:13:06.452 --> 00:13:07.486
[ Laughter ]

00:13:07.486 --> 00:13:08.820
I mean, this is
what he looks like

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:11.323
when he's just trying to read
a prepared statement.

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:15.593
-10,000 known
or "suspested" gang members...

00:13:15.593 --> 00:13:18.730
-"Suspected,"
as in "Robert Mueller suspested

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.033
that Trump obstrusted justice."

00:13:21.033 --> 00:13:22.334
[ Laughter ]

00:13:22.334 --> 00:13:25.871
Again, the report is detailed.

00:13:25.871 --> 00:13:27.306
There's a lot to go through,

00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:28.874
and it will take time
for journalists

00:13:28.874 --> 00:13:30.942
and political systems
to process it.

00:13:30.942 --> 00:13:33.913
But it's worth keeping in mind
that after Barr's first letter,

00:13:33.913 --> 00:13:36.415
Republicans told us it was a
major political win for Trump.

00:13:36.415 --> 00:13:39.051
Compare that to a CNN poll
that found many voters

00:13:39.051 --> 00:13:41.486
felt very differently
about the Russia investigation.

00:13:41.486 --> 00:13:43.522
-Robert Mueller's work is done,

00:13:43.522 --> 00:13:45.557
and among the many
remaining questions,

00:13:45.557 --> 00:13:48.928
how will it weigh on voters
in the 2020 election?

00:13:48.928 --> 00:13:51.896
-So, look, this is a recent poll
we just asked.

00:13:51.896 --> 00:13:54.432
We open-ended it, said, "Okay.
What's the most important issue

00:13:54.432 --> 00:13:57.736
for your 2020 vote?" so voters
could say pretty much anything.

00:13:57.736 --> 00:13:58.871
But look at this.

00:13:58.871 --> 00:14:01.139
Look where
the Russia investigation...

00:14:01.139 --> 00:14:05.176
0% said it was most important
to their vote in 2020.

00:14:05.176 --> 00:14:10.549
Exactly zero, zero, zero
respondents said Russia.

00:14:10.549 --> 00:14:13.485
-Wow. That guy
went full Willie Wonka.

00:14:13.485 --> 00:14:16.655
"Zero! You get nothing!
Good day, sir!"

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:18.123
[ Laughter ]

00:14:18.123 --> 00:14:21.393
So, Mueller laid out the facts,
and now it's up to Congress.

00:14:21.393 --> 00:14:24.129
In fact, there are multiple
specific references to Congress

00:14:24.129 --> 00:14:26.732
in this report, including
one line that is very direct.

00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:28.967
-I just think this sentence
is enormously important.

00:14:28.967 --> 00:14:31.937
-Read it again.
-"The conclusion that Congress

00:14:31.937 --> 00:14:35.040
may apply the obstruction law
to the President's

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:39.110
corrupt exercise of the powers
of office

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:43.415
accords with our Constitutional
system of checks and balances

00:14:43.415 --> 00:14:46.819
and the principle that no person
is above the law."

00:14:46.819 --> 00:14:50.022
This is an invitation
to Congress to say,

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:52.557
"You can do it
using the impeachment power."

00:14:52.557 --> 00:14:54.559
-So, now it's up to Congress
to do their job.

00:14:54.559 --> 00:14:55.794
I don't know if they will,

00:14:55.794 --> 00:14:57.863
but if they did,
the Trump presidency would be...

00:14:57.863 --> 00:14:59.397
-Wrapping up.
-Winding down.

00:14:59.464 --> 00:15:01.400
-Wrapping up.
-Winding down.

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:02.501
This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:15:02.501 --> 00:15:06.705
[ Cheers and applause ]

